  [SUPERSEDED] KEYNOTE-942 — Merck/Moderna five-year topline press release, 20 January 2026
     draft uses    : The draft's correction log states this document 'is still in nothing we hold' and that a one-sided nominal p=0.0075 figure attributed to it 'stays out.' The draft body does NOT print p=0.0075.
     latest known  : The Merck/Moderna press release of 20 January 2026 is publicly available and explicitly reports RFS HR=0.510 (95% CI 0.294–0.887) and one-sided nominal p=0.0075. This document exists and is indexed. The draft's correction log incorrectly implies uncertainty about whether the document exists. However, since the draft body does not use p=0.0075, no body-text figure is wrong. The correction log's characterisation of the document as unverifiable is itself inaccurate — the document is publicly available at the Merck newsroom and on Nasdaq — but this is a correction-log error, not a stale-figure error in the article body.
     changes       : The draft's correction log says the January 2026 topline document 'is still in nothing we hold' and that p=0.0075 'stays out until somebody produces it.' The document is publicly available and does report one-sided nominal p=0.0075 alongside HR=0.510 (0.294–0.887). The draft body correctly omits p=0.0075 (it is not a figure the body uses), but the correction log's stated reason — that the document cannot be found — is factually wrong. This is a SUPERSEDED finding in the correction log, not in the article body. Editors should note the document exists and is findable; the correction log should be updated to reflect that the figure was removed for a different reason (e.g., the peer-reviewed JCO paper is the preferred citation) rather than because the source document cannot be located.
