  [NEW · SERIOUS · FACT] The draft claims KEYNOTE-054 'has posted an overall-survival result that carries no statistical analysis at all,' but the KEYNOTE-054 registry (NCT02362594) shows overall survival as NOT_POSTED with an anticipated posting date of November 2026.
     quote         : “KEYNOTE-054 and KEYNOTE-716 are both pembrolizumab against placebo; each lists overall survival as a secondary endpoint, and each has posted an overall-survival result that carries no statistical analysis at all — no hazard ratio, no confidence interval, no p-value.”
     why           : The KEYNOTE-054 registry record (NCT02362594) lists overall survival reporting status as NOT_POSTED, directly contradicting the claim that a result has been posted. If KEYNOTE-054 has not posted an OS result at all, the sentence is factually wrong about what was released, and the same question applies to KEYNOTE-716. The error matters because it mischaracterises the state of the OS evidence for the comparison arm's drug class — the actual situation (no OS result posted) is more extreme than what the draft describes (an OS result posted without statistics).
     fix           : Replace 'each has posted an overall-survival result that carries no statistical analysis at all' with 'neither has posted an overall-survival result' if that is what the registry records show, or cite the specific conference presentation or publication where each OS result appears and describe what statistical analysis it did or did not carry.

  [NEW · MINOR · THIRD_PARTY] The draft characterises Morning Glory Sciences as 'a site publishing this article in English translation,' implying the original was in another language, without stating what language or offering any evidence for this characterisation.
     quote         : “Morning Glory Sciences — a site publishing this article in English translation, and one we can find no other publication citing”
     why           : The phrase 'in English translation' is a claim about the site's publishing practice — that the article was originally written in another language and translated. No source or language of origin is given. If this is wrong, it mischaracterises the outlet. The draft already discounts the outlet's authority; adding an unverified claim about translation compounds the characterisation without evidence.
     fix           : Remove 'in English translation' unless the original language and translation can be identified, or replace with a neutral description such as 'a site we can find no other publication citing.'

  [NEW · MINOR · CALIBRATION] The draft says the Phase 3 is 'seven times larger' than the Phase 2b, but 1,137 divided by 157 is 7.24, making 'more than seven times larger' the more precise statement.
     quote         : “It is the more trustworthy trial by a wide margin — seven times larger, and blinded against the direction the earlier trial's assessment bias could run in.”
     why           : The ratio is 7.24, so 'seven times larger' understates the difference slightly. In a piece that is precise about every other number, this rounding in the unflattering direction (making the Phase 3 sound smaller relative to the Phase 2b than it is) is a minor calibration issue rather than a material error, but it is the kind of imprecision this publication says it avoids.
     fix           : Change 'seven times larger' to 'more than seven times larger' or 'roughly seven times larger.'

  [NEW · MINOR · CALIBRATION] The draft says the survival analysis rests on 'fourteen deaths, seven in each arm' in the short version summary box, but the same section later clarifies that 'n=14' means fourteen deaths among 157 patients — the summary box does not give the denominator, leaving a reader to wonder whether fourteen is the total patient count or the death count.
     quote         : “14 deaths the whole survival analysis”
     why           : The summary box entry '14 deaths the whole survival analysis' is accurate but compressed. A reader who reads only the summary box does not know that these fourteen deaths are drawn from 157 patients, which is the fact that makes the interval so wide. The body explains this clearly; the summary box does not. This is a calibration issue, not a factual error.
     fix           : Expand the summary box entry to '14 deaths (of 157 patients) the whole survival analysis' or add a parenthetical such as '(7 per arm, 157 patients total).'

  [NEW · MINOR · CALIBRATION] The draft says 'the release says so' about the hazard ratios belonging to KEYNOTE-942, but the short version also says 'the release says so' — these are two separate instances of the same claim and both are accurate, but the second instance in the body section is the one that does the evidential work and should be the one a reader can check.
     quote         : “it does quote hazard ratios, but every one of them belongs to an earlier, smaller trial, and the release says so”
     why           : This is not an error — the Merck/Moderna release does explicitly attribute the hazard ratios to the Phase 2b KEYNOTE-942 five-year data. The claim is accurate. No objection on substance; flagged only because the short version makes this claim without a citation, while the body section provides the supporting detail. This is a structural note, not a correction.
     fix           : No change required. The body section supports the claim adequately.

