  [OVERLAP · MINOR · CALIBRATION] The lower bound of HR 0.165 means the treated group's hazard of death is about 83.5% lower than the control group's — equivalently, about one-sixth of the control rate. That arithmetic is correct. The upper bound of HR 1.345 means the treated group's hazard of death is about 34.5% higher — 'about a third higher' is a reasonable approximation. Both ends are correctly described as rate comparisons. No finding.
